# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — CLIMB 1600
## Build a Complete AI-Powered Competitive Programming Training Platform

Act as a senior product designer, staff full-stack engineer, competitive programming coach, learning-science specialist, AI engineer, and QA engineer.

Build a complete, polished, production-oriented web application named **CLIMB 1600**.

Do not build a landing-page-only prototype, a static dashboard, a collection of mock cards, or a generic chatbot. Build a working personal competitive programming training system with persistent user data, real Codeforces integration, an AI tutor, adaptive problem recommendations, structured learning, contest preparation, analytics, and an anti-procrastination system.

The user is starting from zero and wants to work toward a Codeforces rating of 1600 in 180 days.

The primary objective is to make starting easy, practice deliberate, feedback immediate, and returning after missed days simple.

Do not promise that a particular rating is guaranteed. Optimize the application for measurable learning and progress toward the goal.

