# 7. ADAPTIVE PROBLEM RECOMMENDATION ENGINE

Build a real problem recommendation system.

Use the official Codeforces API where available, particularly:
- problemset.problems
- problemset.recentStatus where appropriate
- user.info
- user.rating
- user.status
- contest.list
- contest.standings when needed for contest analysis

Use only API methods and data fields that actually exist. Verify endpoint parameters against the official Codeforces API documentation.

Official API documentation:
https://codeforces.com/apiHelp

For every recommended problem, display:
- Problem name.
- Contest ID and problem index if available.
- Official Codeforces problem URL.
- Rating, when provided by the API.
- Tags, when available.
- Whether the user has previously solved it.
- Why it is recommended.
- Estimated effort, clearly marked as an estimate.
- Recommended learning objective.

Recommendation logic should consider:
- Current verified rating, if any.
- Baseline skill level.
- Recent accepted and failed submissions.
- Previously solved problems.
- Weak topics.
- Time available.
- Recent problem difficulty.
- Repeated mistakes.
- The user's ability to solve problems without hints.

Use a conservative difficulty progression.

For a complete beginner:
- Start with fundamentals and very accessible tasks.
- Introduce slightly harder tasks only after demonstrating readiness.
- Use a mix of familiar, reinforcing, and challenging problems.
- Increase difficulty when performance supports it, not simply because a calendar week has passed.

For a user who has solved several problems in a topic:
- Increase difficulty gradually.
- Introduce mixed-topic problems.
- Test whether the user can identify the relevant technique independently.

Never label an unverified problem as accepted or solved.

Avoid repeatedly recommending problems the user has already solved unless the purpose is revision.

Provide filters:
- Rating range.
- Tags.
- Solved status.
- Contest.
- Difficulty.
- Estimated time.
- Recommended for me.
- Review mistakes.

Implement caching, request throttling, retries, clear API failure messages, and respect for Codeforces API availability and usage constraints.

Do not scrape Codeforces pages when an official API method is sufficient.

